export anchor WhiteboardStyle:
    number: 114
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Whiteboard
    idea: The dashboard is a dry-erase board in an aluminium frame, written up in four marker colours, with magnets for navigation and faint eraser smudges left behind.
    base: light
    palette:
        wall: #e4e1da, the page behind the board
        board: #fbfcfc, the writing surface, fields and nav labels
        aluminium: #a7aeb5, the frame and the marker tray, decorative only
        blackMarker: #1c2024, text, drawn rules, axes and last week bars
        blueMarker: #1d4fb3, the brand, column heads, names, this week bars, At risk and focus
        redMarker: #bd232b, the overdue circle, Behind and the ring on the current nav label
        greenMarker: #1c6a37, On track, the hours figure and style sheet labels
        ghost: #5d656d, dates, captions and half erased writing
        magnetYellow: #f1c22e, the primary button with black text
    type:
        Two stacks. Hand is Marker Felt, Segoe Print, Bradley Hand,
        Chalkboard SE, Comic Sans MS, cursive, used for the greeting,
        figures, zone titles, project names, statuses, nav and notes. Sans
        is Segoe UI, system-ui, Helvetica Neue, Arial, sans-serif for table
        cells and activity text. Sizes are 44px bold hand for the greeting,
        64px bold hand summary figures, 28px bold hand zone titles, 17 to
        19px hand names and statuses, 15px sans body and 13px sans team
        names.
    layout:
        One whiteboard fills the page inside a 14px aluminium frame with a
        marker tray along the bottom holding four marker pens and an eraser.
        The top row has the blue brand with a starburst mark, six nav labels
        stuck on with round coloured magnets, and on the right a dashed
        marker search box, a yellow pill New project button, a round bell
        with a red count and a green circled MO avatar. The greeting is
        written large with the date tilted in the corner and an arrow
        pointing at 4 tasks are overdue, circled in red marker. The four
        figures are written huge in different marker colours with a double
        underline stroke, split by curved vertical strokes. A long drawn
        line then splits the board into a wide left zone and a narrow right
        zone. The left zone holds a hand ruled project table with hatched
        marker progress bars and the 14 day chart of tilted marker bars,
        black for last week and blue for this week, with values written on
        top. The right zone lists six activity notes with marker icons and
        dashed dividers. Grey blurred smudges sit behind the writing. Below
        860px the zones stack, and below 640px the figures go two by two
        and the table scrolls inside its zone.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px around the board, 20px zone padding, 10px table rows.
    density: Medium. One board, zones split by drawn lines, nothing boxed in cards.
    corners: Uneven hand corners such as 10px 4px 12px 5px on drawn boxes and bars. Round magnets, pill buttons and 6px on the frame.
    borders: 3px marker strokes for the zone dividers and chart axes, 2px for drawn boxes, dashed 2px for the search box and activity rows.
    shadows: Only physical things cast one, the magnets, the nav labels and the frame. The primary button has a 3px hard black lip.
    icons:
        Line icons drawn at a 2.4px stroke in the marker colour. A circled
        tick for On track, a triangle with a mark for At risk, a crossed box
        for Behind and a clock for overdue, always beside the word.
    focus: A 3px blue marker outline offset 3px on every control.
    tone: Friendly team room shorthand, such as Morning, Mara and Latest scribbles.
